                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_76\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit modifies JavaSource/org/unitime/timetable/solver/studentsct/StudentSectioningDatabaseLoader.java, changing:\n\n    for (CourseOffering course: io.getCourseOfferings())\n        section.setName(course.getUniqueId(), c.getClassSuffix(course));\n\ninto a version that only calls section.setName(...) when the class suffix is not null:\n\n    for (CourseOffering course: io.getCourseOfferings()) {\n        String suffix = c.getClassSuffix(course);\n        if (suffix != null)\n            section.setName(course.getUniqueId(), suffix);\n    }\n\nThe fix commit message explains that this null value was later passed into an XML document during passivation/XML export, which is not allowed (adding null text to an XML document throws an error).\n\ncandidate_76 is the commit that originally introduced this exact for-loop and the unguarded `section.setName(course.getUniqueId(), c.getClassSuffix(course));` call into StudentSectioningDatabaseLoader.java (the diff hunk context and line numbers exactly match the pre-fix code shown in fix_commit_diff.txt). No other candidate touches or introduces this specific line in this file \u2014 candidate_78 is actually the fix commit itself, and other matches for \"getClassSuffix\" in candidates (e.g., candidate_10, candidate_39) refer to unrelated code paths (XSection/XClassAssignment models, not this loader method). Since candidate_76 is the sole commit that added the vulnerable, unguarded call, it is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
